meta {
  name: Dependencies
  seq: 1
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  # MTSS > Dependencies
  
  Creates the school and people that certification scenarios need, so tests do not
  depend on the Ed-Fi populated sandbox's students and staff. Run once, in order
  (Dep 1 → Dep 11). Every request is a POST (natural-key upsert), so re-running is safe.
  
  ## Environment prerequisite
  
  Everything hangs under our own school `9999999911`, inside LEA `255901`. The LEA is only
  referenced, never written. The API client must be authorized for LEA `255901` (its
  education organization claims; a 403 lists them). That is the case on ci-v5 and on
  populated-template environments. On an ODS without that LEA, create an LEA, authorize
  the client for it in Admin App / Admin API, and change the LEA id in Dep 1 (the only
  place it appears).
  
  Ed-Fi default descriptors must be loaded (minimal or populated template, or a bulk
  load); the scripts in `Descriptors` only read descriptors, they don't create them.
  
  ## Why there are no "down" scripts
  
  The Foundation is persistent by design. With a relationship-based key (like the CI
  key), a student or staff member can only be deleted while their enrollment or
  assignment exists, and that association blocks the delete (409); deleting the
  association first removes the relationship, so deleting the person returns 403. A
  partial teardown would leave orphaned people and break the next run. Instead the
  Foundation uses reserved identities and is upserted on every run, and the MTSS
  records built on it are fully removed by the MTSS scripts / CI cleanup.
  
  ## Records
  
  | Dep | Resource | Identity |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | 1 | School | 9999999911 under LEA 255901 |
  | 2-3 | Student | 99999911, 99999912 |
  | 4-5 | StudentSchoolAssociation | each student → school 9999999911 |
  | 6-7 | Staff | mtss-staff-01, mtss-staff-02 |
  | 8-9 | StaffEducationOrganizationAssignmentAssociation | each staff → school 9999999911 |
  | 10 | DiagnosisDescriptor | `{{providerNamespace}}/DiagnosisDescriptor#Reading Fluency` |
  | 11 | AttendanceEventCategoryDescriptor | `{{providerNamespace}}/AttendanceEventCategoryDescriptor#Session Not Held` |
  
  Dep 10-11 create descriptors in your provider namespace: set `providerNamespace` in the
  environment to one of the client's namespace prefixes (a 403 "namespace-mismatch" lists them;
  ci-v5 uses `uri://gbisd.edu`).
  
  These identities are reserved for MTSS sample data (SIS will get its own); SIS sample data uses `9999999901`,
  `99999901` and `207220-test01`.
}
